nodecode-arcade is a rewrite of leoresendedop-sys's leoresendedop-sys/hermes-arcade:

  https://github.com/leoresendedop-sys/hermes-arcade
  commit 2daa7bed248a916ed2058f4574d31283a506b571
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Leo (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the original is three surfaces of one plugin - a dashboard
tab (dashboard/dist/index.js and style.css, three HTML5 canvas games with glow,
particles, a WebAudio chiptune synth and an attract mode), a dashboard backend
(dashboard/plugin_api.py, FastAPI routes that persist plays and scores), and an
agent plugin (plugin.yaml, __init__.py, schemas.py, tools.py) whose three tools
answer from the same score store. Here the games themselves are Common Lisp:
Snake is a grid run that ends at a wall or its own body, Breakout a wall, three
lives and a level, Pong a match to seven, each advanced a move at a time and
answering its whole frame as text (games.lisp). The score store keeps the
original's shape and rules - the three games, a play counted when a run starts,
the top ten a game, initials uppercased and cut to three with ??? for none,
best first, filed under the Nodecode home instead of the harness's plugin-data
directory (store.lisp). The three tool answers are the original's, on the same
data: the games with how to play them, the boards with their play counts, and
totals with each game's champion and one player's entries (cell.lisp). The
slash command is the original's /arcade, saying where the cabinet is and
letting the operator play it.

What was left out, and why: the dashboard tab has no counterpart - Nodecode has
no plugin tab to draw a canvas in - so its rendering (glow, scanlines, particle
bursts, screen shake), its chiptune sound, its attract mode with three
autopilots, its arcade-style initials entry dialog, its leaderboard UI and the
Google Fonts import that tab made are all gone; a frame is text and the model
or the operator reads it. The FastAPI backend's HTTP routes go with the tab,
since nothing browses them any more. The attract mode's rule that demo runs
touch no board is not needed here: every run is a run. What the rewrite adds:
arcade_play and /arcade (the seam the tab used to be), the arcade section that
sets initials, the board's length, the grid and the answer's length, and
(help :arcade).
